	(text "1. PWR\n	VDDA3V3 = 3.3 V\n	VDDIO = 1.8 V or 3.3 V. (1.8V is strongly considered)\n\n2. CLK\n	A - PHY is RMII leader\n		25MHz OSC to DP. Chip Generates 50MHz RMII CLK\n	B - RMII follower\n		Gen 50MHz CLK from FPGA and feed\n\n3. Magnetics - ???\n	Look into this, there seems to be some fuckery\n	An option would be using a MagJack (RJ45 w/ Magnetics)\n	Pulse HX1198FNL or something as well?\n\n--- Extra ---\n4. RBIAS - 6.49kOhm\n5. CEXT  - 2 nF\n6. PHY RST -  Have this\n7. MDIO / MDC - Route both prob\n8. ESD Prot - Closest to CONN\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.336 102.362 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "1cee58fc-6908-49b5-a877-3d84a1f9883e")
	)
	(text "Just a heads up:\nSs far I have shown 2 options, DP83826I & DP83822I\nSeems that x26 has been chosen, why? (Curious)\n\nBiggest diff that I found is RGMII support\nThis is important because current ZED implements thru RGMII\nWe would be deviating from that using RMII.\nThis is OK, just making sure it is known, and there is\nplan on how this will be implemented\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 21.844 48.006 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(color 255 0 15 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c5397991-4c97-482d-9a57-73eac209f5c2")
	)
